\b FINITE RELATIONAL SELECTION THEORY - FRST v1.0\b0\par
Frozen independent theory - 2026-09-11\par\par
\b Central proposition\b0\par
Reality is modeled as one finite, relationally constrained quantum system. Space, time, particles, fields, geometry, classical records and probability are treated as organizations or observables of that system rather than separate primitive substances.\par\par
\b Fundamental hierarchy\b0\par
\f1 mathematical possibility -> physical admissibility -> actual universal state/history -> observable reality\f0\par\par
Equivalently, Omega_realized is a subset of Omega_physical, which is a subset of Omega_mathematical.\par\par
\b Twelve frozen axioms\b0\par
1. Finite actuality: 0 < |V| = N < infinity; each primitive identity has a finite-dimensional local state space.\par
2. Relational primacy: primitive labels have no physical meaning apart from invariant relations.\par
3. Completed carrier: once the carrier exists, later evolution does not manufacture additional primitive identities.\par
4. Finite relational structure: a finite relational complex K=(V,E,F,...) carries possible pair and higher relations.\par
5. Constraint selection: physically admissible states satisfy C_alpha |Psi> = 0.\par
6. Complex state principle: coherent alternatives are represented in a complex Hilbert space.\par
7. Closed universal evolution: the complete system evolves within its physical Hilbert space without a fundamental external environment or collapse rule.\par
8. Locality of law: fundamental interactions have bounded relational support or sufficient relational decay.\par
9. Internal time: physical time is reconstructed from subsystem change and correlation, not an external primitive clock.\par
10. Relational geometry: spatial geometry is reconstructed from relational or link state.\par
11. Probability consistency: physical probabilities are normalized, additive on mutually exclusive alternatives and representation/context consistent.\par
12. Observable closure: physically meaningful quantities belong to the invariant physical observable algebra.\par\par
\b Mathematical possibility space\b0\par
For each primitive identity v, let H_v be finite-dimensional. Relations may also carry finite-dimensional state spaces H_e. The raw Hilbert space is\par
\f1 H_raw = (tensor_v H_v) tensor (tensor_e H_e) tensor ...\f0\par
with finite dimension D_raw. A normalized vector or density operator on H_raw is mathematically writable, but not every such state must be physically admissible.\par\par
\b Physical selector\b0\par
Let C_alpha be physical consistency constraints. Define\par
\f1 H_phys = intersection_alpha ker(C_alpha) = P_phys H_raw.\f0\par
P_phys is the orthogonal projector onto the common physical subspace. A state is physically admissible exactly when P_phys |Psi> = |Psi>.\par\par
\b Observable algebra\b0\par
The physical observable algebra is schematically\par
\f1 A_phys = { O = P_phys O P_phys : U_g O U_g^dagger = O }.\f0\par
Gauge transformations are interpreted as changes of relational frame that leave physical observables invariant.\par\par
\b Relational gauge structure\b0\par
If local frames transform independently, a transporter U_ij between identities i and j transforms as\par
\f1 U_ij -> g_i U_ij g_j^{-1}.\f0\par
Closed products W_gamma around relational loops transform by conjugation, so quantities such as Tr(W_gamma) are invariant. Curvature is therefore represented by nontrivial closed relational transport rather than by assuming a continuous gauge field at the fundamental level.\par\par
\b Dynamics\b0\par
The physical Hamiltonian preserves H_phys and is relationally local:\par
\f1 H = P_phys (sum_{X subset K} h_X) P_phys,   [H,P_phys]=0.\par
rho(s) = exp(-isH) rho_0 exp(isH).\f0\par
The parameter s orders the dynamics; physical clock time need not be primitive.\par\par
\b Internal time\b0\par
A clock subsystem C can be correlated with the rest R. A stationary global constraint can yield conditional subsystem evolution when C reads tau. Thus ordered change plus clock correlation can generate effective physical time without an external clock.\par\par
\b Causality\b0\par
Relationally local interactions generate an effective causal cone. Distant observables remain approximately commuting until enough relational evolution has occurred for influence to propagate between their supports. Effective light-cone behavior is therefore an emergent consequence of locality.\par\par
\b Relational geometry\b0\par
For edge-length observables L_e, define\par
\f1 ell_e(rho) = Tr(rho L_e).\par
d_rho(i,j) = min over paths gamma from i to j of sum_{e in gamma} ell_e(rho).\f0\par
Geometry can therefore change while the primitive carrier remains fixed. Cosmic expansion is not identified with creation of new primitive identities.\par\par
\b Effective dimension\b0\par
A graph or relational Laplacian Delta_rho can define an effective spectral dimension through return probabilities. Four-dimensional spacetime is then a possible intermediate-scale property rather than a fundamental assumption.\par\par
\b Fields and continuum\b0\par
Fields are coarse collective observables of many relational degrees of freedom. A continuum theory is an effective large-scale approximation to the finite relational system, with controlled error as the observational scale becomes large compared with the primitive relational scale. Physical infinity is not required as an ontological premise.\par\par
\b Matter, charge and mass\b0\par
Stable excitation sectors of the physical Hamiltonian represent matter. Conserved symmetry-sector labels represent charges. If E_0 is the ground energy and E_1 is the first admissible excited energy, the spectral excitation cost is\par
\f1 Delta = E_1 - E_0 > 0.\f0\par
At an effective relativistic level this can be represented as m c_eff^2 = Delta.\par\par
\b Measurement and probability\b0\par
Measurement is modeled as unitary correlation of system, apparatus and environment. Decoherence can produce stable approximately classical records without introducing a fundamental collapse law. Under the standard finite-dimensional quantum probability assumptions, probabilities take the form\par
\f1 p(P) = Tr(rho P).\f0\par
For a pure state and one-dimensional outcome projector this gives the Born form |c_a|^2.\par\par
\b Classicality and thermodynamics\b0\par
Classical facts are stable, redundantly recorded relational information. Global unitary entropy can remain constant while subsystem/coarse entropy grows through entanglement and information redistribution. Irreversibility is therefore effective rather than a fundamental loss of universal information.\par\par
\b Gravity and singularities\b0\par
Geometry and matter are degrees of freedom in the same global relational system. A successful low-energy limit must reproduce the observed gravitational equations with controlled corrections. Literal continuum singularities are not fundamental objects in a finite carrier with finite-dimensional local state spaces and bounded physical generators; instead they signal breakdown of the continuum approximation.\par\par
\b Completed creation versus history\b0\par
The primitive carrier K=(V,E,F,...) can remain fixed after completion while rho changes. Thus finished creation is mathematically compatible with continuing history, changing geometry, structure formation, decay and relational expansion.\par\par
\b Master FRST object\b0\par
\f1 R_FRST = (K, H_raw, P_phys, A_phys, H, rho_0, observables).\f0\par
Observable reality is generated from this one constrained relational system.\par\par
\b Frozen boundary\b0\par
FRST v1.0 is an architecture, not an experimentally established theory of our universe. It does not yet determine the numerical carrier, local dimensions, exact constraint family, exact Hamiltonian/couplings, or actual initial/boundary state. Its deepest unresolved specification problem is why one particular triple (P_phys, H, rho_0), or an equivalent unified law, is selected rather than another.\par\par
FRST v1.0 assumes finite actuality. That assumption must not be imported into Unified Coherence Dynamics as a theorem. The UCD VS FRST comparison instead tests whether UCD can derive a corresponding finite-realization result from its own source law and whether that source law forces the specific Q72/H504/H-net architecture.\par
